{"type":"npc","name":"Sepsis Serpent","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":95,"temp":0,"max":95,"details":"void healing"},"ac":{"value":21,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":15}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"critical-hits","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]},{"type":"visual","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"acid","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"slashing","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["necril","venenan"],"details":""},"level":{"value":6},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Sepsis serpents are intelligent hunters who spend much of their time lurking inside small cracks or inside corpses, ready to pounce on the first creature that comes near them. When prey approaches, they strike fast, infesting the victim with their venom. If the victim seems particularly strong and healthy, a sepsis serpent might also inject a tiny clone of itself into the target's bloodstream as insurance against defeat. Once injected, the tiny clone remains inert, but it primes itself to quickly mature into a new sepsis serpent upon its host's death. Sepsis serpents do not tolerate competition for prey, and offspring that don't quickly retreat and cede their host's corpse are soon devoured by their parent.</p><p>As sepsis serpents age and feed, they steadily grow in size, with more potent toxins to match. The first sepsis serpents were said to have originated centuries ago from an awakened snake that was cursed to die from his own poison. According to legends, these first serpents are now large enough to swallow up an elephant in a single gulp.</p><h2>Persistence of Memory</h2><p>When a sepsis serpent dies and a new one coagulates from its venom, the new serpent retains the memories of the elder. It is aware of the elder's enmities and alliances, and it inherits its elder's treasures and long-term plans. Nevertheless, the serpent considers itself a new individual, and usually takes a new name. It generally doesn't hold a grudge against its elder's killers, and it might even reward them for allowing it to take its elder's place.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 30/65/125 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Deception, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, death, dexterity, energy resistant (acid, void), fortification, intelligence, poison, poisonous armor, spiked, throwing, unholy, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Juho Kattelus","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":2},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":3},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":13,"senses":[{"type":"motion-sense","acuity":"precise","range":60}],"vision":false},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":15,"special":[]},"athletics":{"base":12,"special":[{"label":"to Grab","predicate":["action:grab"],"base":14}]},"deception":{"base":12,"special":[]},"stealth":{"base":15,"special":[]}},"traits":{"value":["ooze","poison","undead","unholy"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"_id":"ey7HjiwkdozbK6Ih","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/sepsis-serpent.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Sepsis Serpent","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/sepsis-serpent.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offset